Overview
This practical demonstrates time-series forecasting using a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) neural network. 
Historical gold prices are used to create sequences, which are then provided to the LSTM model to predict the next gold price.

Dataset
The Gold Price Dataset contains historical daily gold prices.
Dataset: Gold Price Dataset
Source: Kaggle
Feature used: Date and INR gold price
Target: Gold price in INR
Data type: Time-series
Frequency: Daily
The Date column represents the date of the observation, while the INR column contains the corresponding gold price in Indian Rupees.

Sequence Creation
A sequence length of 30 days is used.
The previous 30 gold prices are used as input to predict the gold price of the next day.

LSTM Model
The model consists of:
LSTM layer with 50 units
Dense output layer with 1 neuron
The model uses:
Optimizer: Adam
Loss function: Mean Squared Error
Epochs: 10
Batch size: 32
LSTM is suitable for time-series forecasting because it can learn patterns and dependencies from sequential data.
